    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining our offensive attack. His score of 73.66 is the clear high-water mark, bolstered by a 14% platoon advantage against Brandon Pfaadt and favorable park factors. We are also leaning heavily into our middle infield and corner spots, specifically **Gunnar Henderson** (67.24) and **Coby Mayo** (65.57). Both benefit from a 16% park boost against Robert Gasser, and we have specifically adjusted their outlooks to account for Gasser\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a statistically significant \"green light\" environment for their respective stolen base profiles. **Jackson Merrill** (64.10) also remains a core staple today; his ability to leverage a 13% platoon edge against Eury P\u00e9rez helps him retain a high floor despite a slightly unfavorable park adjustment.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Miguel Vargas**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a score of 52.55. While **Miguel Vargas** benefits from a strong xwOBA of .378 and an assumed lead-off spot that grants him a +10% order bonus, the optimizer preferred the superior matchup context of **Nasim Nunez** (52.13), whose SP skill metrics and switch-hitting versatility narrowly edged out the volume argument for **Miguel Vargas**. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while **Liam Hicks** (41.38) hangs on as a marginal start; he sits just above our bench threshold, but we are keeping a close eye on the official lineups to ensure he retains that #4 spot.\n\nRisk mitigation remains paramount as we navigate a day where almost every confirmed lineup is still pending. **Drake Baldwin** (63.45) carries a high score, but that assumes he occupies the #1 spot; should the lineup shift him down, his value will degrade rapidly. We are also wary of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** facing a lefty in Gasser\u2014while the park and delivery variables mitigate the platoon risk, any late-game defensive substitutions or pinch-hit scenarios could cap their counting stats. Outside of the active roster, we are holding firm on the bench status of **Brayan Rocchio** and **Wade Meckler**, as their profiles do not offer the ceiling required to displace our current starters. We will proceed with the current configuration, banking on the speed and platoon efficiency of our primary core to maintain our standing in a tight 5x5 race.",
